# 007-threading-clock: asio any_executor type-erasure ref-count race
#
# asio::detail::ref_count_down uses fetch_sub(memory_order_release) + a
# manual atomic_thread_fence(acquire) on the last decrement (a classic
# shared_ptr-style refcount optimisation — atomic_count.hpp). The pattern
# is CORRECT but TSan cannot always establish happens-before across the
# manual fence, so it flags races in shared_target_executor<T>::~impl()
# when a custom executor (e.g. fixpp::core::session_executor) is erased
# into asio::any_io_executor and its any_executor copy is dropped on a
# thread other than the one that constructed it (co_spawn on
# session_executor → strand on a multi-thread io_context, US4 seam 6 et al).
# Affects asio 1.36.0; not a fixpp::session_local concurrency issue (the
# slot is plain value ownership, read on the strand — race-free).
race:asio::execution::detail::shared_target_executor
race:asio::execution::detail::any_executor_base
